{
    "word": "yggdrasil",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "68891d4e-f1f8-3ce1-bf23-97a33462b263",
                "word": "Yggdrasil",
                "pos": "name",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "80c87d09-d7da-3fe1-9692-b8db36fc0060",
                        "entry_id": "68891d4e-f1f8-3ce1-bf23-97a33462b263",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An immense ash tree that is central in Norse cosmology, believed to connect the nine worlds."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Norse"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9d14dd87-8e55-4eb6-91eb-e7b117cfa8ef",
                                "sense_id": "80c87d09-d7da-3fe1-9692-b8db36fc0060",
                                "text": "Yet it is not easy to pluck out the heart of its mystery; and the descriptions of certain ancient representatives of Yggdrasil do not lessen the difficulty."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ef3a5afc-f469-4973-bca3-0bbb10fc70a7",
                                "sense_id": "80c87d09-d7da-3fe1-9692-b8db36fc0060",
                                "text": "With nostrils and legs akimbo, she towered over him like some human Yggdrasill, blotting out the sun."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6006054c-7285-4314-bc27-02fb3f840c04",
                                "sense_id": "80c87d09-d7da-3fe1-9692-b8db36fc0060",
                                "text": "1996, Carolyne Larrington (editor and translator), The Seeress's Prophecy, The Poetic Edda, page 6,\nI know that an ash-tree stands called Yggdrasill,\na high tree, soaked with shining loam;\nfrom there come the dews which fall in the valley,\never green, it stands over the well of fate."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "469a1b2a-e5f1-4597-8905-4d2b28b8e8e0",
                                "sense_id": "80c87d09-d7da-3fe1-9692-b8db36fc0060",
                                "text": "In Norse mythology, for example, the World Tree, or Yggdrasil, connected the nine existences that straddled the worlds of gods and men with its mighty roots. Yggdrasil was reputedly a gigantic ash tree (and was the central feature of Norse cosmology), around the base of which the serpent Níôhöggr had twisted its body."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2e97f9f0-f66b-4df2-902f-59c4d13f962c",
                                "sense_id": "80c87d09-d7da-3fe1-9692-b8db36fc0060",
                                "text": "“Yggdrasil!” Gudbjartur's voice was filled with awe. “It is Yggdrasil, the world-tree!” He looked at Halfdan, his eyes wide. “The Sacred Grove is here in this land!”"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "96157834-c6a7-402c-ae0b-600124c1434a",
                        "source_entry_id": "68891d4e-f1f8-3ce1-bf23-97a33462b263",
                        "source_sense_id": "80c87d09-d7da-3fe1-9692-b8db36fc0060",
                        "source_sense_description": "the world tree in Norse mythology",
                        "target_lang_word": "Yggdrasil",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Yggdrasil",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7fb2d2e3-4fd5-3018-b4f2-35f9a98bced2",
                                        "entry_id": "3acb7488-8b64-38b0-93d3-3c953694f870",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Arbre-Monde de la mythologie nordique."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Mythologie nordique"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "915e56ff-c80b-4f13-b3a5-fbf2c68ca07e",
                                                "sense_id": "7fb2d2e3-4fd5-3018-b4f2-35f9a98bced2",
                                                "text": "Je connais un frêne, on le nomme Yggdrasill,\nArbre chevelu, humecté par un nuage brillant,\nD’où naît la rosée qui tombe dans les vallons ;\nIl s’élève, toujours vert, au-dessus de la fontaine d’Urd."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "03a2c60f-c2d6-4b39-a969-7ee12dbd232f",
                                                "sense_id": "7fb2d2e3-4fd5-3018-b4f2-35f9a98bced2",
                                                "text": "Les Nornes, bien que leur sourire soit amer,\nPuisent à la fontaine où s’abreuve Mimer\nUne eau qui me fit sage, et, de cette eau féconde,\nBaignent pieusement l’immense arbre du monde.\nIl remplit l’univers : comment donc mourrait-il,\nLe vieux Frêne, l’aïeul vénérable, Yggdrasil ?\nEt, tant qu’il survivra, quel péril nous menace ?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "12d6452f-f731-49cc-8f45-81a34f4ee4c7",
                        "source_entry_id": "68891d4e-f1f8-3ce1-bf23-97a33462b263",
                        "source_sense_id": "80c87d09-d7da-3fe1-9692-b8db36fc0060",
                        "source_sense_description": "the world tree in Norse mythology",
                        "target_lang_word": "Yggdrasill",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Yggdrasill",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ba200d2e-b6be-38ec-a862-737c6d62f444",
                                        "entry_id": "0d5a7dd7-5539-301c-b29a-94f682c36cf0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Variante d’Yggdrasil, arbre de vie de la mythologie nordique."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Mythologie nordique"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "79b184a3-6394-4b22-be20-176f9ac3524e",
                                                "sense_id": "ba200d2e-b6be-38ec-a862-737c6d62f444",
                                                "text": "La gloire du soleil sur leur face rayonne,\nComme au jour où tu vis le monde nouveau-né\nDu déluge sanglant sortir illuminé ;\nEt toujours Yggdrasill, à sa plus haute cime,\nDes neuf sphères du ciel porte le poids sublime."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "aea2f27b-45c4-49b8-9510-029c9cc5aab4",
                                                "sense_id": "ba200d2e-b6be-38ec-a862-737c6d62f444",
                                                "text": "Univers éternel, arbre toujours vivant,\nYggdrasill, frêne énorme aux vibrantes ramures.\nQuel esprit est en toi, quel grand souffle et quel vent,\nVient t’émouvoir sans fin, et t’emplir de murmures ?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4b001e5f-3d2a-418c-a530-2b8763521a1a",
                        "source_entry_id": "68891d4e-f1f8-3ce1-bf23-97a33462b263",
                        "source_sense_id": "80c87d09-d7da-3fe1-9692-b8db36fc0060",
